# Summary
    This project has the purpose of comparing three algorithms for solving the 0/1 Knapsack Problem explained in class.
    To compile the project write this command in a terminal inside this directory:
        
        make
    
    By running this command, the whole project will be compile and build a binary file, named "knapsack"
    To run this file write one of the commands in a termnal inside this directory:

        ./knapsack -X
        ./knapsack -E=n
    
    The binary file can receive two parameters:

        "-X" is for running "Demonstration Mode". It generates a random 0/1 Knapsack Problem and shows the solutions
        of the three algorithms. At the end the program creates a pdf file with the solutions and opens evince to show
        the pdf file in presentation mode.

        "-E=n" is for running "Experiment Mode". It will generate 100n random problems, where "n" must be a positive integer.
        These problems will be solved using the three algorithms and at end the program will create a pdf file with the results 
        of the experiment and open with evince in presentation mode.